This drops the old import path. A couple of forks still subclass it from here: FlagScale (deepseek_transformer_layer.py, on their Megatron-LM-FL fork) and miles (deepseek_v4_1.py, on radixark/Megatron-LM miles-main), so they'd hit an ImportError on their next upstream sync.

Not a big deal since mHC isn't in any release yet, but a lazy re-export is pretty cheap IMO:

    def __getattr__(name):
        if name == "HyperConnectionTransformerLayer":
            from megatron.core.transformer.hyper_connection_transformer_layer import (
                HyperConnectionTransformerLayer,
            )
            return HyperConnectionTransformerLayer
        raise AttributeError(f"module {__name__!r} has no attribute {name!r}")

